obs r1 crux on metal: the successor's own three fresh keys signing their coronation refuse NotMember — a set cannot crown itself; only the outgoing roll hands authority forward. Eight scenes GREEN first build.
obs r3 modeled the Knot as a succession chain with checkpoint pruning: a party holding only a trusted anchor roll forward reaches the identical head as one who walked from genesis; four broken-link refusals (NotMember/BelowQuorum/DigestMismatch/StaleEpoch).
obs r4 true-to-the-bytes: std.debug.print writes to stderr, so the sha256sum cross-check needed `2>&1 |` (learned from muster_true's witness idiom); the system sha256sum of the canonical roll bytes equals the digest the warrant carries and every validator signed — two tools, one answer. fmtSliceHexLower is absent in this Zig std; used the module's own to_hex.
obs No red booked — all four rungs GREEN on first or second build; TAME style + width clean throughout. A served warrant reaches the Comlink-served custody gate (stayed the maintainer's hand).
